{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["<b>And I entreated HaShem.</b> Seven names are given for prayer, and they are: tefillah, techinah, tze'akah, za'akah, nefilah, pegi'ah, rinah. And in all of them Moses did not pray except by way of techinah. And why? Because at the time Moses said before the Holy One, blessed be He: 'Make me know Your ways — by what measure do You guide Your world?' — the Holy One, blessed be He, said to him: ״וחנותי את אשר אחון״ — that is to say, all that I do with them is a gift of grace that I give them. Moses said to Him: by that very measure that You told me — conduct Yourself and give me as a gift of grace that I may cross the Jordan. Therefore it says ואתחנן — the language of וחנותי. Another explanation: Moses prayed 515 prayers, the numerical value of ואתחנן."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:00:26.345776844Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}